  "findings": [
   "at equal size the in-register grid decode (tbl) costs about as much as the gathers: 69-72 vs 78-80 GB/s at one token; it wins only when the decode is amortized over 2-4 tokens (+4 to +30 %)",
   "rp (+12 % memory) is +4-6 % at one token and +14-43 % at 2-4 tokens over gather",
   "expanded codes double the rate (IQ2_XXS 115-125, IQ1_S 110-120 GB/s source-equivalent) but cost 61-64 % more memory: IQ1_S then has Q2_K's size and speed, so neither expanded layout is a useful format",
   "IQ1_S has no compact gather-free form (2048-entry grid = 64 svtbl tables)"
  ],
  "simulator": "ds41f.py IQ2_XXS width curve = best equal-size kernel per width (gather at 1 token, tbl at 2-4): 77.5 / 56.5 / 50.3 / 45.7 GB/s -> 1 / 1.372 / 1.541 / 1.696; absolute one-token rates stay from job 52438878 so formats remain comparable within one session"
 },
